# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# MasterFabric monorepo — environment overview
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# This repo uses per-package env files. Copy the examples below into each app.
#
#   mf-go/.env.example     →  mf-go/.env
#   mf-expo/.env.example   →  mf-expo/.env.development (and .env / .env.local as needed)
#
# Optional repo root file `local.env` is loaded by mf-expo/app.config.js (overrides)
# so you can keep machine-specific GraphQL URLs outside mf-expo.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── mf-go (backend) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# See: mf-go/.env.example
# Minimum local: DATABASE_DSN, REDIS_ADDR, JWT_SECRET (≥32 chars for prod)
# OTP email: OTP_DELIVERY=email + SMTP_* (Mailpit in mf-go/deployments/docker-compose.yml)

# ── mf-expo (Expo app) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# See: mf-expo/.env.example
# Point GraphQL at mf-go:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_DEV_GRAPHQL_URL=http://localhost:8080/graphql
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_GRAPHQL_URL=http://localhost:8080/graphql
